;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The $depth call's first instruction: (global.get 0)
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; The callee's body is ((:GLOBAL.GET 0) (:CONST (:I32) 4) (:BINOP (:I32) (:DIV (:U))))
; and the first instruction reads global 0 -- SP -- through the callee's own
; frame.  The step is lifted through the whole stack in the project's recipe:
;
;   dgread-slice   the lone read (the split rule's value (const (:i32) sp));
;   dgread-ctxt    the context step at the callee's body;
;   dgread-step    the step bridge;
;   dgread-label   the callee's label 1;
;   dhread-frame   the callee's frame, at the OUTER state pair (the frame rule
;                  runs the inner body at (%;% ($sof sp) C2), which is the
;                  callee pair, so the frame's own step fact is at the inner
;                  shape and this one is the frame rule at the halt level);
;   dhread-ctxt    the context step at the halt body (the frame at the head,
;                  the rest of the branch spliced back);
;   dhread-label   the halt block's label 0;
;   dhread-labelctxt  the context step at label 1's body (label 0 at the head,
;                  the rest of the dispatch after it);
;   dhread-label6  function 6's label 1;
;   dhread-outer   function 6's frame 6, through dstep-frame-outer-gen.
;
; The pair has two spellings again: the frame rule writes the inner state as
; (%;% ($sof G1) C2), so the facts below are at that spelling and
; dh-pair-spelled is disabled (enabling it folds the pair into dcallee-pair and
; the frame rule's inner state no longer matches).  The component selectors
; dh-sof-of-pair/dh-fof-of-pair reduce ($sof SP) and ($fof SP) in the outer
; fact without unfolding the store.
;
; Total: 2.18M prover steps for the chain, the outer link 28.5k.

