;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The inner abort ifelse: the else branch, at the literal-0 body
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; The halt branch's inner ifelse is
;
;   (if (eqz (call $depth)) (then (call $abort) (return)))
;
; so when the depth is nonzero, eqz gives 0 and the ELSE branch is taken (an
; empty block).  The ifelse's condition is the testop's value, symbolic in sp;
; rather than carry that value through every search, the whole chain is proved
; at the LITERAL-0 body -- ((const 0) (ifelse ...) rest) -- where every search
; evaluates.  A bridge (dif-*, next section) rewrites the actual body's testop
; value to 0 with the depth-nonzero hypothesis.
;
; The chain mirrors the testop's: dif0-slice (the pure if-false rule),
; dif0-prefix7, dif0-ctxt-abs/dif0-ctxt (with prefix7 as a hypothesis),
; dif0-s141-7/8, dif0-spure, dif0-split, dif0-step (through
; dstep-phases-gen), dif0-label, dif0-labelctxt, dif0-label6, dif0-outer.
;
; ONE GENERATION NOTE, because it cost a round: the body must be written as an
; EXPLICIT cons of the ifelse onto the rest -- (cons (const 0) (cons ifelse
; rest)) -- not as (cons (const 0) (cddr ...)).  The chain term normalizes
; differently inside the search's take/nthcdr slices and the context proof
; then stalls; the explicit cons goes through.  Total: 750k steps.

