;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The empty block, and the empty label's dissolve
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; The inner abort ifelse's else branch is (block (:_result nil) NIL); its step
; is the read rule Step_read/block, and the label it becomes dissolves by
; Step_pure/label-vals.  Both chains are at TEQ-free bodies and mirror the
; earlier ones: prefix7, ctxt-abs/ctxti, the search nils, spure, split, step
; (through dstep-phases-gen), label, labelctxt, label6.  Also proved here:
; %size-is-acl2-count (7 steps), the bridge that lets the frame rule's size
; premises evaluate.
;
; OPEN: the two *-outer facts (the frame-6 lifts).  The wrapper's conditional
; size hypothesis is not being discharged: ACL2 ends up with the NEGATION of
; the size inequality as a goal -- (<= (+ 8902 (acl2-count (fof ...))) 8896)
; -- even though the positive form is a proven, evaluated fact (dblk-size).
; The wrapper's instance conclusion and the goal term appear identical, so the
; next diagnosis is a term-level diff of the instance against the goal
; (:brr on the wrapper's application, or proving the abstract conclusion with
; the inner step and the size inequality as hypotheses and comparing).

(defthm %size-is-acl2-count (equal (w3t::%size x) (acl2-count x)) :hints (("Goal" :in-theory (enable w3t::%size))))

