; The frame-6 lifts of the block and label steps.  The obstacle was one of my
; own: the outer fact's right-hand side had been written (list (list config))
; instead of (list config) -- emit wraps step facts in a list, and the chain
; passed an already-wrapped result -- so the wrapper's conclusion never matched
; the goal and ACL2 chased the negated size hypothesis.  With the RHS as the
; bare config, both go through in ~23k steps, with acl2-count-of-frame-gt-body
; (a generic fact: a frame's instruction list is bigger than its body) and
